{"title":"Career Roadmap · Insolvency Analyst","role":"Insolvency Analyst","summary":"An Insolvency Analyst supports insolvency professionals, law firms, creditors, financial institutions, resolution applicants, turnaround teams and other stakeholders in analysing financially distressed companies and insolvency proceedings.","facts":{"Current degree":"Law - LLB / BA LLB / BBA LLB / B.Com LLB / B.Sc LLB (Integrated)","Course":"Insolvency & Bankruptcy Law"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An Insolvency Analyst supports insolvency professionals, law firms, creditors, financial institutions, resolution applicants, turnaround teams and other stakeholders in analysing financially distressed companies and insolvency proceedings."},{"type":"p","text":"The role combines:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Insolvency law"},{"text":"Corporate law"},{"text":"Finance"},{"text":"Accounting"},{"text":"Legal research"},{"text":"Due diligence"},{"text":"Financial analysis"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Case management"}]},{"type":"p","text":"In India, insolvency work commonly involves the Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code (IBC) framework, insolvency professionals, adjudicating authorities, creditors' committees and resolution processes."},{"type":"p","text":"An Insolvency Analyst is generally a support and analytical professional, not automatically an Insolvency Professional. Formal insolvency-professional roles have separate statutory eligibility, examination, registration and experience requirements."}]},{"heading":"Career Pathway","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Integrated LL.B","Insolvency & Bankruptcy Specialisation","Insolvency / Restructuring Internship","Legal / Insolvency Analyst","Insolvency Analyst","Senior Insolvency Analyst","Insolvency / Restructuring Associate","Insolvency & Restructuring Manager","Senior Insolvency Professional / Specialist"]},{"type":"p","text":"Possible law-firm pathway:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Law Student","Dispute Resolution / Insolvency Intern","Insolvency Legal Associate","Senior Associate","Insolvency & Restructuring Specialist","Partner / Practice Head"]}]},{"heading":"What Does an Insolvency Analyst Do?","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An analyst helps understand what happened to a distressed company, what assets and liabilities exist, what creditors are owed, what legal proceedings are pending, and what possible resolution or recovery options exist."},{"type":"h","text":"Typical Responsibilities"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Analyse insolvency cases"},{"text":"Research insolvency law"},{"text":"Review company records"},{"text":"Analyse creditor claims"},{"text":"Study financial statements"},{"text":"Review contracts"},{"text":"Conduct legal due diligence"},{"text":"Track court/NCLT proceedings"},{"text":"Prepare case chronologies"},{"text":"Analyse creditor positions"},{"text":"Assist with resolution plans"},{"text":"Review claims documentation"},{"text":"Prepare research notes"},{"text":"Support insolvency professionals and legal teams"},{"text":"Track statutory and procedural timelines"},{"text":"Prepare case reports and presentations"}]}]},{"heading":"Insolvency Case Lifecycle","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Financial Distress","Default","Insolvency Proceedings","Admission / Commencement","Resolution Professional / Process Administration","Claims Collection & Verification","Committee of Creditors","Information Memorandum","Resolution Plans","Evaluation","Approval / Implementation","OR"]},{"type":"p","text":"Liquidation"},{"type":"p","text":"The exact process depends on the type of proceeding, applicable law and orders of the relevant authority."}]},{"heading":"Year-by-Year UG Roadmap","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Legal & Business Foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Build fundamentals in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Legal methods"},{"text":"Contract law"},{"text":"Constitutional law"},{"text":"Torts"},{"text":"Economics"},{"text":"Business studies"},{"text":"Accounting fundamentals"},{"text":"Legal research"},{"text":"Legal writing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Start Learning"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"What is insolvency?"},{"text":"What is bankruptcy?"},{"text":"What is financial distress?"},{"text":"What is a creditor?"},{"text":"What is a debtor?"},{"text":"What is default?"},{"text":"What is liquidation?"},{"text":"What is restructuring?"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Finance Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Assets"},{"text":"Liabilities"},{"text":"Equity"},{"text":"Revenue"},{"text":"Expenses"},{"text":"Profit"},{"text":"Cash flow"},{"text":"Debt"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Corporate & Commercial Law"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Company Law"},{"text":"Contract Law"},{"text":"Property Law"},{"text":"Partnership"},{"text":"Sale of Goods"},{"text":"Civil Procedure"},{"text":"Commercial transactions"},{"text":"Corporate governance"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Financial Skills"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn how to read:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Balance sheets"},{"text":"Income statements"},{"text":"Cash-flow statements"},{"text":"Annual reports"},{"text":"Debt schedules"},{"text":"Auditor reports"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Practical Exercise"},{"type":"p","text":"Take a listed company's annual report and identify:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Assets","Liabilities","Borrowings","Cash Flow","Profitability","Potential Financial Stress"]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Insolvency Specialisation"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Insolvency law"},{"text":"Corporate insolvency"},{"text":"Liquidation"},{"text":"Debt restructuring"},{"text":"Creditor rights"},{"text":"Secured vs unsecured creditors"},{"text":"Insolvency procedure"},{"text":"Resolution plans"},{"text":"Avoidance transactions"},{"text":"Recovery mechanisms"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Indian Insolvency Ecosystem"},{"type":"p","text":"Become familiar with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code"},{"text":"Insolvency and Bankruptcy Board of India"},{"text":"National Company Law Tribunal"},{"text":"National Company Law Appellate Tribunal"},{"text":"Insolvency professionals"},{"text":"Resolution professionals"},{"text":"Creditors' Committee"},{"text":"Financial creditors"},{"text":"Operational creditors"},{"text":"Resolution applicants"},{"text":"Liquidators"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Students should verify the latest statutory provisions, regulations, circulars and procedural requirements before relying on them professionally."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 4 — Financial & Legal Analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"For a five-year integrated law program, develop stronger analytical capabilities."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Corporate distress analysis"},{"text":"Financial restructuring"},{"text":"Debt restructuring"},{"text":"Credit analysis"},{"text":"Legal due diligence"},{"text":"Resolution-plan analysis"},{"text":"Liquidation analysis"},{"text":"Asset recovery"},{"text":"Insolvency litigation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced Finance"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Debt-equity ratios"},{"text":"Current ratio"},{"text":"Interest coverage"},{"text":"EBITDA"},{"text":"Working capital"},{"text":"Cash conversion"},{"text":"Debt service"},{"text":"NPA concepts"},{"text":"Enterprise value"},{"text":"Recovery value"}]}]},{"heading":"Final Year — Professional Insolvency Practice","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Work on practical cases involving:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Insolvency petitions"},{"text":"Creditor claims"},{"text":"Resolution plans"},{"text":"Liquidation"},{"text":"Avoidance transactions"},{"text":"Related-party transactions"},{"text":"Fraudulent transactions"},{"text":"Preferential transactions"},{"text":"Undervalued transactions"},{"text":"Wrongful trading concepts"},{"text":"Asset recovery"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Final-Year Goal"},{"type":"p","text":"The student should be able to answer:"},{"type":"p","text":"Why is the company distressed, who are the stakeholders, what claims exist, what assets are available, what legal proceedings are underway, and what resolution/recovery options are possible?"}]},{"heading":"Core Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Skill Area","Skills"],"rows":[[{"text":"Insolvency Law"},{"text":"IBC framework, CIRP, liquidation"}],[{"text":"Corporate Law"},{"text":"Companies, directors, governance"}],[{"text":"Legal Research"},{"text":"Statutes, regulations, case law"}],[{"text":"Financial Analysis"},{"text":"Statements, ratios, cash flow"}],[{"text":"Credit Analysis"},{"text":"Debt, default, creditor exposure"}],[{"text":"Due Diligence"},{"text":"Legal and financial review"}],[{"text":"Resolution"},{"text":"Resolution plans, restructuring"}],[{"text":"Litigation"},{"text":"NCLT/NCLAT-related work"}],[{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Claims, notices, reports"}],[{"text":"Research"},{"text":"Case precedents and regulatory updates"}],[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Financial and case analysis"}],[{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Reports and presentations"}],[{"text":"Technology"},{"text":"LegalTech and financial analytics"}]]}]},{"heading":"Insolvency Analyst Workflow","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Case Identification","Company & Industry Research","Financial Analysis","Legal Due Diligence","Creditor / Claim Analysis","Case Law & Regulatory Research","Asset & Liability Mapping","Resolution / Recovery Analysis","Report Preparation","Senior Review","Case Monitoring"]}]},{"heading":"Important Concepts to Master","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Corporate Insolvency"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Default"},{"text":"Insolvency p